In article <1992Apr24.223021.12093@midway.uchicago.edu> wen5@midway.uchicago.edu writes:
>In article <1992Apr22.183523.11282@news.cso.uiuc.edu> act31797@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu (The Procrastinator  P1000) writes:
>>I'm having trouble with running nethack on a PC.  I get the game to execute
>>OK, but instead of printing the screen it just prints lots of garbage (with
>>some normal text intertwined).  I think the problem is with the termcap.
>
>The termcap library can't do anything without a screen device.  In this case,
>use DOS's ansi.sys in your config.sys file as:
>device=c:\dos\ansi.sys (or whatever path it resides within)
>
>There is another ansi driver called nansi.sys that can be obtained from
>wuarchive.  It is used similarly to ansi.sys, except that you must set
>the environment variable TERM under DOS to nansi-color or nansi-mono:
>set TERM=nansi-mono
>
>You might want to create a batch file nh.bat that has these two statements:
>set term=ansi-color (or whatever term you need)
>nethack
>
>Hope that helps.
>
>Stan T2 Wen


Also, add these lines to autoexec.bat or to the batch file that calls
nethack:

set termcap=\nethack\termcap 
set term=ansi         


Notice that there is no "c:" in the termcap variable, just the
pathname, no drive letter. This cost me a few hours of irritation.
Maybe it's just the compilation I have, but the one I have definitely
won't work if i set termcap=c:\nethack\termcap.

Of course, substitute the directory where you have put the nethack
files, and the terminal you have, if other than ansi.

